  <p>Copy and reveal are plain buttons: Tab to focus, Enter or Space to activate. The <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code> takes <code>tabindex="0"</code> so long lines can be scrolled from the keyboard.</p>
  <p>Live terminal: click anywhere in it (or Tab to it) to focus the prompt. <kbd class="dd-kbd">Enter</kbd> runs the line, <kbd class="dd-kbd">↑</kbd> / <kbd class="dd-kbd">↓</kbd> walk through history (it starts with the commands already on screen), <kbd class="dd-kbd">Tab</kbd> completes a known command or lists the matches — and when there is nothing to complete, Tab moves focus on as usual, so the terminal never traps it. <kbd class="dd-kbd">Ctrl</kbd> <kbd class="dd-kbd">L</kbd> clears, <kbd class="dd-kbd">Ctrl</kbd> <kbd class="dd-kbd">C</kbd> abandons the line. Output is read out through a polite live region; the mirrored line is hidden from screen readers because the input carries the value.</p>

  <h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
  <Guides
    do={['Name the file in the bar when the snippet belongs somewhere.', 'Highlight the one or two lines the reader should look at.', 'Mask secrets by default and copy the real value.', 'Keep prompts (<code>$</code>) out of the copied text: wrap each command in <code>dd-code__input</code>.', 'Keep playback short — two or three commands with real output — and let it rest on a prompt.', 'Give a live terminal a script for the commands people will try, with a description each for <code>help</code>.']}
    dont={['Don’t wrap code lines in block elements inside <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code> — copy gets blank lines.', 'Don’t use a terminal block for source files; it is for commands and output.', 'Don’t colour whole lines to show syntax — tokens only. Status colours go on output lines, not commands.', 'Don’t colour the window dots red, yellow and green; they are quiet tones, not buttons.', 'Don’t autoplay more than one terminal per view, or loop it.']}
  />
